-- title:
--   Γ̃-translation of an even rigidification, with exact level transport
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $k_0$ denotes the residue quotient $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ (in Lean, `Onr ⧸ Ideal.span {algebraMap 𝒪 Onr π}`), and "rigidification" means a term of `FakeEllipticCurve.Rigidification r π A₀ ψ E`, i.e. a fake elliptic curve $E_b$ over $B/\pi B$ realised as the pullback of $E$, a fake elliptic curve $A_b$ over $B/\pi B$ realised as the pullback of $A_0$ along the residue leg of $\psi$, together with $g_b$, $g_A$, an exponent $d$ and a pair $\varphi,\varphi'$ exhibiting $E_b\to A_b$ as a level-preserving isogeny pair of degree $r^d$.
--
--   **Numerical and coefficient data.** Primes $r$ and $\bar r$ and a level $N\neq 0$ are given, with $\bar r\neq r$, $r\nmid N$, $\bar r\nmid N$ and $N$ squarefree. The ring $\mathcal O$ is a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain (`hdvr`) with $\pi$ irreducible, $\pi$-adically complete (`hcomplete`), residue field of cardinality $r$ (`hres`) and $(r)=(\pi)$ (`hunr`); $K_0$ is its fraction field. The ring $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is a characteristic-zero $\mathcal O$-domain with an $\mathcal O$-automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, complete for the ideal $(\pi)$ (`hOnr_complete`), with $(\pi)$ maximal (`hOnr_max`), every element a root of a monic $\mathcal O$-polynomial modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial of positive degree having a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $\mathrm{Fr}(x)\equiv x^{r}\pmod{\pi}$ (`hFr`). The homomorphism $\mathrm{vdet}:\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) is characterised by `hvdet`: $\mathrm{vdet}(g)=n$ exactly when $\det g$ is a unit of $\mathcal O$ times $\pi^{n}$.
--
--   **Indefinite side and moduli.** $a,b\in\mathbb Q$ are such that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ is indefinite and ramified exactly at $r$ and $\bar r$ (`hB`), and $\Lambda$ is a maximal order in it (`hΛ`). The scheme $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with the point assignment `pt` is a coarse moduli space for fake elliptic curves with $(\Lambda,N)$-structure (`h𝒳`: invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with pullback, bijectivity on algebraically closed fields, and the universal property). An auxiliary level $n\ge 3$ is fixed with $r\nmid n$, $\bar r\nmid n$ and $\gcd(n,N)=1$; $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with `ptF` is a fine moduli space at full level $n$ (`hM`), carrying an action $\rho$ of a group $G$ with labels $\chi:G\to\Lambda$ which is a level-twist action (`hρ`: the automorphisms are over the base, they realise the $\chi(g)$-twists on full level structures, and $\chi$ is a bijective labelling modulo $n$). The forgetful map $p:M\to\mathcal X$ is over the base (`hp`), is $G$-invariant (`hρp`) and matches the two point assignments (`hp_pt`). For each prime $\ell\notin\{r,\bar r\}$ a coarse moduli space $\mathcal Y_\ell$ with extra level $\ell$ is given (`h𝒴`), with structure maps $g_\ell$, point assignments `ptT`, and two degeneracy maps $d_0,d_1:\mathcal Y_\ell\to\mathcal X$ over the base (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`) computing respectively the underlying curve (`hd₀`) and the quotient by the extra level (`hd₁`). Atkin–Lehner endomorphisms $a_r,a_{\bar r}$ of $\mathcal X$ over the base (`harf`, `harbarf`) realise the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$ on points (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **Definite side.** Rationals $a_1,b_1$ are such that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ is definite and ramified exactly at $\bar r$ (`hdef`); $\Lambda_1$ is a maximal order, $R_1\le\Lambda_1$ an Eichler order of level $N$, $n_1$ an adelic element of the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$, and $\mathrm{meetOrder}(R_1,n_1)$ an Eichler order of level $Nr$ (`hS₁`). An injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map $\iota_0$ into $M_2(K_0)$ is fixed, together with the place $v$ above $r$. The subgroup $\tilde\Gamma=\Gamma_t$ is exactly the group of units of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ integral with respect to $R_1$ at all places other than $v$ (`hΓt`). Hecke elements $s_\ell$ (global) and $s\!f_\ell$ (adelic) are given for each prime $\ell\notin\{r,\bar r\}$ with: $s\!f_\ell$ equal to $s_\ell$ at all places away from $r$, equal to $1$ at $r$, the product of the idelic diagonal of $\ell$ with $s\!f_\ell^{-1}$ lying in the level Hecke set of $(\Lambda_1,\mathrm{meetOrder}(R_1,n_1))$ at $\ell$ when $\ell\mid N$ and in the prime Hecke set of $\mathrm{meetOrder}(R_1,n_1)$ at $\ell$ otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell)=\ell$ (`hs`); the groups $\Gamma_{t,\ell}$ are the intersections $\Gamma_t\cap s_\ell\Gamma_t s_\ell^{-1}$ (`hΓtℓ`). An element $\bar w$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma_t$ is given (`hwbar`). Finally $\Lambda$ contains all rational integers (`hΛℤ`), and `coord` is an order coordinate system for $\Lambda$ at $r$ (`hcoord`: additive, sends $1$ to $(1,0)$, multiplicative in the twisted Witt sense, injective, $r$-adically dense, and compatible with reduced traces).
--
--   **Special fibre.** Over $k_0$ there are: a fake elliptic curve $A_0$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$ (`hX₀`), formal coordinates $\theta_0$ of rank $2$ on $A_0$ presenting $A_0$ as a formal module via `coord`, $X_0$ and $\theta_0$ (`hA₀`), families $e_\gamma,e'_\gamma$ of endomorphisms of $A_0$ indexed by $\gamma\in\Gamma_t$ with $e_\gamma$ over the base (`he`) and degree exponents $\deg\gamma$. The hypotheses on this family are: each $(e_\gamma,e'_\gamma)$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving the $N$-level (`hE1`); multiplicativity up to powers of $r$ (`hE1mul`); scalars $\gamma$ act, up to powers of $r$, as the corresponding integer (`hE1sc`); conversely, if $e_\gamma$ is an integer multiplication up to a power of $r$ then $\gamma$ is a scalar (`hE1'`); for every injective ring homomorphism from the centraliser of the $X_0$-action and $\varpi_{X_0}$ into $M_2(K_0)$ there is a conjugator $g$ such that every $\gamma$ has a germ $\varepsilon$ computing $e_\gamma$ in the coordinates $\theta_0$ on all nilpotent test data, with image $r^{k_\gamma}g\iota_0(\gamma)g^{-1}$ (`hE2`); the level-$n$ labelling $\mathrm{lab}:\Gamma_t\to\Lambda$ of the action of $e_\gamma$ on a given full level structure, multiplicative and normalised on scalars modulo $n$ (`hE3`); and the lifting property (`hE4`): over an algebraically closed $k_0$-algebra, every level-preserving $r$-power isogeny endomorphism of a pullback of $A_0$ comes, up to powers of $r$, from some $e_\gamma$. A further order $R_2\le R_1$ (`hR₂`, `hR₂o`, `hR₂r`) carries endomorphisms $\hat e_x$ over the base (`hê`) which are additive, $\Lambda$-equivariant and level-preserving (`hE5a`), unital and multiplicative and compatible with integers (`hE5b1`–`hE5b3`), satisfy the norm relation $\hat e_{\bar x}\hat e_x=[\mathrm{nrd}\,x]$ (`hE5c`), agree with $e_\gamma$ up to powers of $r$ when $x=r^{k}\gamma$ (`hE5d`), and admit a simultaneous matrix realisation with the $e_\gamma$ (`hE5e`).
--
--   **Drinfeld side.** A ring homomorphism $\iota$ from the Witt ring $\mathbb Z_{r^2}$ into $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is given, together with a special formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ of height $4$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/r$ (`hΦ`, `hΦ4`), a moduli package $\mathrm{MD}$ satisfying the Zariski sheaf condition (`hMD`), and a comparison $\eta$ from rigidified objects to $\mathrm{MD}$ which, on Noetherian bases with $r$ nilpotent, separates admissible rigidified objects exactly up to isomorphism, is natural in the base, and is locally surjective on a distinguished open cover (`hη`, three clauses). An injective $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $\Phi$-action and $\varpi_\Phi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ is given whose image is commensurable with $M_2(\mathcal O)$ in the precise sense of `hE₀`. The comparison $e_D$ identifies the functor $\mathcal G(\mathcal O,\mathrm{MD})$ with the product of $\mathrm{Spec}\,O^{\mathrm{nr}}$-points and Deligne data: it is natural (`hnatD`), bijective on every Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra with $\pi$ nilpotent (`hbijD`), compatible with the $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$-leg (`hfstD`), translates the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$-action into the twisted action `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` (`hGLD`), translates $\pi$-translation into the Frobenius twist on the first factor (`hPiD`), and $\pi$-translates exist (`hPiexD`). Moreover $\kappa$ reduces $k_0$ to $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/r$ compatibly with the quotient maps (`hκ`), and $\beta_0$ is an isogeny from $\Phi$ to $X_0\otimes\kappa$ of height $4n_0$ (`hβ₀`).
--
--   **Base point, Atkin–Lehner datum at $\bar r$, and the comparison $\Xi$.** A full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$ is fixed. A second curve $A_{0,w}$ over $k_0$ with maps $a_w,a_w'$ exhibiting the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ (`hALw`) and $b_w,b_w'$ an isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$ preserving level (`hBSw`, `hBSwlev`) is given, such that the composite $a_w\!\!\;b_w$ has a germ realising $\iota_0(\bar w)$ up to a power of $r$, simultaneously with the germs of the $e_\gamma$ (`hJOINTw`). The assignment $\Xi$ sends a rigidified curve over a Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent to a point of $\mathcal G(\mathcal O,\mathrm{MD})$; it has Frobenius-twisted $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$-leg over connected bases (`hΞleg`), is natural in the base (`hΞnat`), is insensitive to isomorphisms of rigidified curves up to $r$-powers (`hΞiso`), and is computed by $\eta$ on an admissible rigidified transport with shift $j\le 1$ (`hΞdef`).
--
--   **Equivariance and the Cherednik–Drinfeld dictionary.** With a fixed conjugator $g_0\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$: translating a rigidification by $e_\gamma$ moves $\Xi$ by $Z^{c}g_0\iota_0(\gamma)g_0^{-1}$ for some $c\in\mathbb Z$, where $Z$ is the central scalar $r$ (`heqΓ`); the analogous statement holds for the Atkin–Lehner datum at $\bar r$ and $\bar w$ when $\bar r$ is invertible in the base (`heqW`). The four clauses `hK1`–`hK4` provide, over connected Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras with $\pi$ nilpotent: existence of an even rigidified curve with prescribed image $(\psi,P)$ under $g_0^{-1}$-twisted action (`hK1`); uniqueness of such a curve up to an isomorphism compatible with the rigidifications (`hK2`); compatibility with base change along $\mathcal O$-algebra maps (`hK3`); and a deformation statement along a surjection whose kernel squares to zero in the stated sense (`hK4`). The clauses `hC0e` and `hC0u` give existence and uniqueness of the height-normalised transported level-$n$ structure `IsNormLevelTransport` attached to a rigidification and to $P_0$. Finally $\Theta_f$ is a natural transformation into the nilpotent points of $M$ (`hnat`), equivariant for the $G$-action (`hG`), whose first component computes the fine moduli point of $(E,P_n)$ (`hC2`) and, after composing with $p$, the coarse moduli point of $E$ (`hC2c`).
--
--   **Transported matrix realisation and the slack character.** An injective $E_X$ from the centraliser of the $X_0$-action and $\varpi_{X_0}$ into $M_2(K_0)$ is given, linked to $E_0$ through $\beta_0$ and a quasi-inverse $\beta_0'$: $\beta_0'$ is an $\mathcal O_D$-homomorphism (`hβ₀'`) with $\beta_0'\circ\beta_0=[r^{N_\beta}]_\Phi$ and $\beta_0\circ\beta_0'=[r^{N_\beta}]$ on $X_0\otimes\kappa$ (`hβ₀'β₀`, `hβ₀β₀'`), and every germ $\varepsilon_X$ transports to a germ for $\Phi$ with $E_0$-image $r^{N_\beta}E_X(\varepsilon_X)$ (`hEXE₀`). For $E_X$ a conjugator $g_X$ is fixed together with germs $\varepsilon_\gamma$ computing $e_\gamma$ in the coordinates $\theta_0$ and exponents $k_\gamma\in\mathbb Z$ with $E_X(\varepsilon_\gamma)=r^{k_\gamma}g_X\iota_0(\gamma)g_X^{-1}$ (`hεk`). A homomorphism $\mathrm{slack}:\Gamma_t\to(\mathbb Z/n)^\times$ records $r^{k_\gamma}$ modulo $n$ in the form $\mathrm{slack}(\gamma)\,r^{(-k_\gamma)^+}=r^{(k_\gamma)^+}$ in $\mathbb Z/n$ (`hslack`), and a homomorphism $\theta_t:\Gamma_t\to G$ satisfies $\chi(\theta_t\gamma)\cdot e_\gamma(P_0)=\mathrm{slack}(\gamma)\cdot P_0$ as points of $A_0$ (`hθt`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under these hypotheses the following holds. Let $B$ be a Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra in which $\pi$ is nilpotent and whose only idempotents are $0$ and $1$, let $\psi:O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to B$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra map, let $P$ be a Deligne datum over $B$, let $E$ be a fake elliptic curve with $(\Lambda,N)$-structure over $B$ and let $\varrho$ be a rigidification of $E$ relative to $A_0$ along $\mathrm{frobTwist}(-\mathrm{vdet}(g_0))\psi$, such that the $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$-leg of $\Xi(E,\varrho)$ equals $\mathrm{frobTwist}(-\mathrm{vdet}(g_0))\psi$ (evenness) and $e_D(\Xi(E,\varrho))$ is carried to $(\psi,P)$ by the $g_0^{-1}$-twisted action. Let $\gamma$ be a unit of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ lying in $\Gamma_t$, and let $\psi'$, $P'$ be such that $(\psi,P)$ is carried to $(\psi',P')$ by the action twisted by $\iota_0(\gamma)$, that is, $\psi'=\mathrm{frobTwist}(-\mathrm{vdet}(\iota_0\gamma))\psi$ and $P'$ is the pullback of $P$ under $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}$. Then there exists a rigidification $\varrho'$ of the same curve $E$ relative to $A_0$ along $\mathrm{frobTwist}(-\mathrm{vdet}(g_0))\psi'$ such that:
--
--   (i) the $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$-leg of $\Xi(E,\varrho')$ equals $\mathrm{frobTwist}(-\mathrm{vdet}(g_0))\psi'$, i.e. $\varrho'$ is again even;
--
--   (ii) $e_D(\Xi(E,\varrho'))$ is carried to $(\psi',P')$ by the $g_0^{-1}$-twisted action;
--
--   (iii) for all full level-$n$ structures $P_n$ and $P_n'$ on $E$ that are height-normalised transports of $P_0$ along $\varrho$ and along $\varrho'$ respectively, one has $P_n'=\chi(\theta_t\gamma)\cdot P_n$, an identity of points, the action being that of $E$ on its points through $\Lambda$;
--
--   (iv) for every prime $\ell\neq r$ with $\ell$ invertible in $B$, for every extra level structure at $\ell$ on $A_0$ (the Lean binder reuses the name `K₀`) which is stable under $e_\gamma$ in the sense that points factoring through its level subscheme are sent by $e_\gamma$ to points again factoring through it, and for all extra level structures $C,C'$ at $\ell$ on $E$ such that $C$ is compatible with $\varrho$ and $C'$ with $\varrho'$ — meaning that every point of $\varrho.E_b$ (resp. $\varrho'.E_b$) which factors through $C$ (resp. $C'$) after composition with $g_b$ has its image under $\varrho.\varphi$ followed by $g_A$ (resp. $\varrho'.\varphi$ followed by $g_A$) factoring through the chosen extra level structure of $A_0$ — the subschemes $C$ and $C'$ cut out the same points: for every scheme $T$, every $T\to\operatorname{Spec}B$ and every point $R$ of $E$ over it, $R$ factors through $C$ if and only if it factors through $C'$.
--
--   This is the $\tilde\Gamma$-translation step in the Cherednik–Drinfeld uniformisation of the Shimura curve attached to an indefinite quaternion algebra ramified at $r$ and $\bar r$: it converts the translation of a point of the Drinfeld symmetric space by an element $\gamma$ of the arithmetic group $\tilde\Gamma$ into a second even rigidification of the same fake elliptic curve, with the height-normalised transported level-$n$ structure moved exactly by the label $\chi(\theta_t\gamma)$ and with all extra level structures away from $r$ unchanged. It is used in the construction of the $\tilde\Gamma$-equivariant identification of the formal fibre of the fine moduli space at full level $n$ with the formal Drinfeld upper half plane.
